course: dictionary
lesson: 13389
title: Words that show feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Look at the word in two parts: heart and less. Less means without, as in careless or useless. So heartless means without a heart, which here means without kindness.
explain: «The king was heartless. He took the villagers' bread and left them hungry.» Taking food from hungry people is cruel, so heartless must mean cruel and unkind. Try your meaning in the sentence: «The king was cruel and unkind» still makes sense.
explain: Ask yourself what word would fit. If you can put in cruel or unkind and the sentence still works, you have found the meaning.
fact: Heartless means cruel and unkind, not caring about other people's feelings.
fact: «A heartless act» is something unkind that someone does, without caring how it makes others feel.
fact: «How heartless!» is what you say when someone has been very unkind.
fact: Heartless is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like a heartless king or a heartless thing to say.
fact: The opposite of heartless is kind or caring.
exercise: «It was a heartless thing to laugh when Sam fell over and cut his knee.» What does heartless mean? | *Cruel and unkind | Loud and noisy | Quick and clever | Very funny
exercise: «Mia helped the lost puppy find its way home.» Is Mia heartless? | Yes, she was too clever | *No, she was kind and cared about the puppy | Yes, she found the puppy's home
exercise: «The heartless king took the villagers' food.» Find and copy the word that tells you what kind of king he was. | *heartless | villagers | food | king
test: «How heartless!» said Ben, when nobody stopped to help the girl who dropped her shopping. What does heartless mean here? | Very tidy | Very tall | *Very unkind, not caring about her | Very quiet
test: Which sentence shows a heartless act? | Two friends read a book together | The girl shared her sweets with her friend | *Someone laughed at a boy who was crying over his lost dog | The family planted a tree in the park
exam: Jayden says heartless means heart-shaped. Is he right? | No, it means very hungry | Yes, it means full of love | Yes, it means heart-shaped | *No, heartless means cruel and unkind, not heart-shaped
